  "worked_solution": "From the adjacent intervals rule, we know that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{2}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,+\\,{\\int }_{5}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,=\\,{\\int }_{2}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nPlugging in the known information gives\n\n$$\n4+(-6)\\,=\\,{\\int }_{2}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\u21d2\\,{\\int }_{2}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-2.\n$$\n\nFinally, compute the desired integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{9}(3-2f(x))\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{2}^{9}1\\,\\text{d}x\\,-\\,2{\\int }_{2}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\cdot x{|}_{2}^{9}\\,-\\,2(-2) \\\\  & =3(9-2)+4 \\\\  & =21+4 \\\\  & =25\\end{aligned}\n$$",
